WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.000
Inherited changes in one sodium-channel gene can remove pain or cause severe pain

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.400
syndromes. That is strong causal evidence for a channel in human pain, and a reason

3
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.620
to target it with drugs.

4
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.220
Three families in northern Pakistan had members who had never experienced pain.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.140
They had two broken copies of SCN9A, the gene for Nav1.7.

6
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.180
In cultured cells, their mutant channels passed no current above background.

7
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.400
Other variants in the same gene cause pain syndromes.

8
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.940
Some channels open at more negative voltages and close more slowly.

9
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.920
Others fail to inactivate properly, leaving persistent sodium current.

10
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.100
Same gene, different channel defects, different pain phenotypes.

11
00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:56.613
Nociceptor spikes draw on Nav1.7, Nav1.8, and Nav1.9.

12
00:00:57.453 --> 00:00:59.153
The first two contribute to the spike.

13
00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:04.353
Nav1.9 mainly sets resting potential and subthreshold excitability.

14
00:01:05.393 --> 00:01:07.853
More channel function need not mean more firing.

15
00:01:08.813 --> 00:01:14.633
Some human Nav1.9 variants depolarized rat sensory neurons enough to impair spike

16
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:15.633
generation.

17
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.887
The drug story went differently.

18
00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:25.667
A selective Nav1.7 blocker did not significantly beat placebo in a trial of painful

19
00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.027
diabetic neuropathy.

20
00:01:28.027 --> 00:01:30.007
Suzetrigine blocks Nav1.8.

21
00:01:30.847 --> 00:01:35.207
It reduced pain after surgery versus placebo in both phase 3 trials.

22
00:01:36.147 --> 00:01:39.927
These were different pain conditions, not a direct comparison of targets.

23
00:01:40.627 --> 00:01:46.147
Neither surgery trial demonstrated superiority over hydrocodone with acetaminophen.

24
00:01:47.047 --> 00:01:53.127
Approval in the United States followed in January 2025 for moderate-to-severe acute

25
00:01:53.127 --> 00:01:54.127
pain in adults.

26
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.010
The neurons themselves are diverse.

27
00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:02.290
A molecular label, a conduction class, and a functional state describe different

28
00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.650
things. A label does not fix a stimulus function.

29
00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.330
Nociceptors can change state through sensitization.

30
00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.610
In cultured mouse sensory neurons, nerve growth factor brought out mechanical

31
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.970
currents that required PIEZO2.

32
00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:20.003
One smaller point closes the story.

33
00:02:20.903 --> 00:02:26.063
In dissociated adult human sensory neurons, suzetrigine generally reduced repetitive

34
00:02:26.063 --> 00:02:28.303
firing without eliminating it.

35
00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:31.083
Blocking a channel is not neuronal silence.

36
00:02:31.963 --> 00:02:34.103
The clinical trials measured pain relief.
